course: dictionary
lesson: 9504
title: Stern: a face, a boat, a warning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The stern teacher did not smile once.» Stern means serious and strict here, because a teacher who does not smile is being serious. Ask: what word would fit? Strict fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Stern can also be a noun, meaning the back part of a ship or boat. «The sailors sat at the stern and waved.» Boats and sailors are the clues, so stern means the back of the boat. Check by swapping in back part: it still makes sense.
explain: Stern can also describe a hard, serious warning. «The coach gave a stern warning before the match.» A warning is not a joke, so stern tells you it was serious and firm. Toad's words fade when «he sees their stern faces», because serious faces make him stop talking.
fact: Stern means serious and strict, not smiling.
fact: The stern is the back part of a ship or boat, and the bow is the front.
fact: A stern warning is a serious, hard warning.
fact: Stern faces in old photos do not always mean a person was cross: people were expected to look serious in photos, and Queen Victoria often looks stern in them, yet her diaries show she laughed and enjoyed jokes.
exercise: «The stern teacher did not smile once.» What does stern mean here? | *Serious and strict | Kind and funny | Wet and cold | The back part of a boat
exercise: «The sailors sat at the stern and waved goodbye.» Where did the sailors sit? | In the sea | At the front of the boat | Under the deck | *At the back of the boat
exercise: «Toad's words fade when he sees their stern faces.» What do the faces show? | *The others look serious and strict | The others are very tired | The others are laughing at Toad | The others are asleep
test: «The coach gave a stern warning before the match.» What is a stern warning? | A kind hug | A quiet, funny joke | A warning about the weather | *A serious, hard warning
test: Mia says a stern look is just a sad look. Why is she not quite right? | She is right, there is no difference | Stern is only a word for ships | Stern and sad mean exactly the same | *Stern means serious and strict, not just sad
exam: In which sentence does stern mean the back part of a boat? | «The stern teacher frowned.» | «Give a stern warning.» | *«The crew sat at the stern.»
